---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { siteSettings } from '../lib/site';
const contact = siteSettings().contact;
---
<Layout title="Privacy — Who Goes First?" description="Player names stay on your device. Learn about optional group memory, preferences, clean sharing, and this version’s lack of tracking."><div class="content-page prose"><h1>Privacy</h1><p class="lede">The picker runs on your device. Names and results are not sent to a server.</p><h2>What this version stores</h2><p>Preferences use your browser’s local storage under <code>wgf:preferences:v1</code>: reveal choice, sound and motion settings, input mode, and a schema version. Names, seat order, and stable player IDs are saved only if you turn on “Remember this group.” We don’t store results or a history of picks.</p><p>Saved information stays until you forget it or clear this site’s browser data. Under Preferences, “Forget this group” clears the roster and returns to four seats. “Reset settings” resets preferences and stops remembering the current group. If storage is blocked, the picker works in memory and explains that changes may not persist.</p><h2>What leaves your device</h2><p>Loading a public website sends ordinary connection information, such as your IP address and requested page, to its host. This local version has no public hosting service configured. A public release must identify its host and review that host’s logging settings.</p><p>There are no third-party scripts, ads, analytics requests, cookies, AI calls, accounts, or session recording in this build. Searches are filtered on your device and are not logged. Publisher source links open an external website only when you follow them; that website has its own privacy practices.</p><h2>Sharing</h2><p>“Share” shares or copies a clean link. It removes query strings and fragments and includes no names, group settings, or winner. Your browser or operating system handles its own sharing interface.</p><h2>Questions</h2><p>{contact ? <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>Contact the owner</a> : 'An owner contact address and public hosting details must be added before launch.'}</p><p class="small muted">Implementation policy · 19 September 2026. Changes to data collection require a separate review.</p></div></Layout>

